From b923f21115d6ae3e10fea15f40802abe483805c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:27:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A striker's weight goes into its blow: tipped forward a
 moment as the blow lands (patch 0077)

A struck body already leans back along the blow; the striker stood bolt upright through its own
swing. When an action clip reaches its impact keyframe (where the script is told the blow landed),
the striker now tips forward over its feet, out fast and settling over 0.35 s, as a struck lean
does: 0.06 rad for a quick blow, up to 0.1 for a wind-up of 0.6 s or more. It is the existing lean
tilt, about the same pivot over the feet, along the unit's facing; it doesn't start over a roll or
a struck lean already turning the body, on a reaction, or on an upper body swinging over running
legs. `actionWeight` (benilla's own, registered "1") turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
